=== TITLE: USG Right Hemithorax / Chest (Right) ===
=== IMPRESSION ===
NORMAL RIGHT THORACIC ULTRASOUND STUDY.
- No pleural effusion, subpleural consolidation, or pneumothorax in right hemithorax.

=== FINDINGS ===
STUDY: HIGH-RESOLUTION THORACIC ULTRASONOGRAPHY (RIGHT HEMITHORAX)

OBSERVATIONS:
- RIGHT PLEURAL LINE: Smooth, thin, and continuous with normal lung sliding movement.
- RIGHT PLEURAL CAVITY: Clear costophrenic sulcus without evidence of pleural effusion.
- RIGHT LUNG: Normal peripheral lung parenchymal pattern. No consolidation or mass.
- RIGHT HEMIDIAPHRAGM: Normal position, contour, and smooth respiratory excursion.